---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import CtaBanner from "../../components/CtaBanner.astro";
import { sitePath } from "../../lib/url";

const title = "Case Studies: Startup Raises Run With Rupert | Rupert";
const description =
  "How Rupert ran real raises end to end: the financial model, investor targeting and outreach. Our clients stay anonymous; the numbers and the work are real.";

// Clients stay anonymous at their request. Add a case by adding an entry here.
const cases = [
  {
    id: "healthcare-seed",
    round: "seed",
    tag: "Seed · Healthcare · US & Canada",
    title: "A $2M Seed round for a first-time founder in healthcare",
    facts: [
      { label: "Round", value: "$2M" },
      { label: "Stage", value: "Seed" },
      { label: "Sector", value: "Healthcare" },
      { label: "Geography", value: "US & Canada" },
      { label: "Investors targeted", value: "50+" },
      { label: "Timeline", value: "3 months, end to end" },
    ],
    result: "Round closed in full",
    situation: [
      "A first-time founder who had never raised before and didn't know where to start: what investors expect, what to say to them, or how a raise actually runs.",
      "The company was real, but its story wasn't there yet. There was no clear narrative an investor could follow from first email to decision.",
    ],
    steps: [
      {
        title: "Built a clear understanding of the company",
        body: "Worked through the business with the founder: the market, the model and what makes it investable, so it could be explained the way investors need to hear it.",
      },
      {
        title: "Rebuilt the financial model",
        body: "Rebuilt the model from the ground up, so the numbers behind the story could stand up to investor questions.",
      },
      {
        title: "Built the narrative and the one-pager",
        body: "The full investor story, from the problem to why this team and why now. Shaped the one-pager that led the outreach, and gave detailed feedback on the deck.",
      },
      {
        title: "Ran the entire process",
        body: "Targeting across more than 50 investors, then structured outreach and follow-up, guiding the founder through each step of a process they had never run before.",
      },
    ],
    quote:
      "I didn't know where to start. Having a structured, organized approach is what really led to consistent outreach, and to results.",
    quoteBy: "Founder, healthcare company, US & Canada",
  },
  {
    id: "pet-care-series-b",
    round: "series-b",
    tag: "Series B · Pet care · US",
    title: "A $100M Series B for a US pet-care company",
    facts: [
      { label: "Round", value: "$100M" },
      { label: "Stage", value: "Series B" },
      { label: "Sector", value: "Pet care" },
      { label: "Geography", value: "US" },
      { label: "Investors targeted", value: "~25" },
      { label: "Timeline", value: "3 months, end to end" },
    ],
    result: "Round closed in full",
    situation: [
      "The company had outgrown its investor network. A $100M round meant going to a new kind of investor: institutional funds it had no relationships with.",
      "Those investors also brought a very different due diligence process, with a much higher bar for reporting, data quality and professionalism. The company's financial model was a simplified one that couldn't answer the questions they would ask. The team wasn't ready for that level of scrutiny.",
    ],
    steps: [
      {
        title: "Rebuilt the financial model",
        body: "Replaced the simplified model with a full one, built to answer the questions institutional investors ask before they commit.",
      },
      {
        title: "Got the company diligence-ready",
        body: "Brought reporting, data and materials up to the standard a $100M round is judged against.",
      },
      {
        title: "Found the right investors",
        body: "Identified and prioritized about 25 investors that fit the round's size, stage and sector, instead of spraying a long list.",
      },
      {
        title: "Designed and ran the outreach",
        body: "A focused, personal approach: roughly one email per target, aimed at getting the meeting, then supporting the founder through the conversations that followed.",
      },
    ],
    quote:
      "The work took the company to a new level. It started with what investors demanded, and it changed how we manage and operate the company: in a different, data-driven way.",
    quoteBy: "CEO & Founder, US pet-care company",
  },
  {
    id: "sustainable-finance-series-a",
    round: "series-a",
    tag: "Series A · Sustainable finance · US",
    title: "A $10M Series A for a US sustainable-finance company",
    facts: [
      { label: "Round", value: "$10M" },
      { label: "Stage", value: "Series A" },
      { label: "Sector", value: "Sustainable finance" },
      { label: "Geography", value: "US" },
      { label: "Reorganization", value: "2 months" },
      { label: "Timeline", value: "4 months, end to end" },
    ],
    result: "Round closed in full",
    situation: [
      "The company wanted to raise, but its numbers wouldn't survive an investor's first look. Headcount had grown well ahead of the business, large expenses weren't needed, and there was no clear view of how, or when, it would break even.",
      "A better model alone wouldn't fix that. The company itself had to change before it could raise.",
    ],
    steps: [
      {
        title: "Reorganized the company",
        body: "Over two months, brought the cost base back to what the business needed: a reduction in force, and the unnecessary expenses cut.",
      },
      {
        title: "Rebuilt the financial model",
        body: "In parallel, a new model and a new financial view of the company, with a clear answer to how and when it breaks even.",
      },
      {
        title: "Put new operating protocols in place",
        body: "New operational protocols for how the leaner company runs, so the numbers investors saw were the numbers it actually operated on.",
      },
      {
        title: "Ran the raise",
        body: "With the company reorganized and the numbers credible, took it to investors and closed the round: four months from start to money in.",
      },
    ],
    quote:
      "Without Dori and the reorganization of the company, with its focus on cost cutting, burn and runway, we wouldn't be here today.",
    quoteBy: "CEO, sustainable-finance company, US",
  },
];

// Round filter: one button per round that has a case, in this order.
const roundOrder = [
  { id: "seed", label: "Pre-Seed & Seed" },
  { id: "series-a", label: "Series A" },
  { id: "series-b", label: "Series B" },
];
const rounds = roundOrder.filter((r) => cases.some((c) => c.round === r.id));
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonicalPath="/case-studies/">
  <main id="main-content" class="flex-1">
    <section class="site-wrap py-2xl lg:py-3xl">
      <p class="cs-eyebrow">Case Studies</p>
      <h1 class="type-h1 mt-md">Real raises, run with Rupert.</h1>
      <p class="type-body-lg mt-lg max-w-prose">
        Our clients stay anonymous. The numbers and the work are real.
      </p>
    </section>

    <div class="site-wrap pb-xl">
      <div class="cs-rounds" role="group" aria-label="Filter case studies by round">
        {
          rounds.map((r, i) => (
            <button type="button" class="cs-round" data-round={r.id} aria-pressed={i === 0 ? "true" : "false"}>
              {r.label}
            </button>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </div>

    {
      cases.map((c) => (
        <section class="site-wrap pb-2xl lg:pb-3xl cs-section" id={c.id} data-round={c.round} aria-labelledby={`${c.id}-title`}>
          <article class="cs-case">
            <header class="cs-head">
              <p class="cs-eyebrow">
                {c.tag}
              </p>
              <h2 id={`${c.id}-title`} class="type-h2 mt-sm">
                {c.title}
              </h2>
            </header>

            <dl class="cs-facts">
              {c.facts.map((f) => (
                <div class="cs-fact">
                  <dt>{f.label}</dt>
                  <dd>{f.value}</dd>
                </div>
              ))}
              <div class="cs-fact cs-fact--result">
                <dt>Result</dt>
                <dd>{c.result}</dd>
              </div>
            </dl>

            <div class="cs-body">
              <div>
                <h3 class="type-h3">The situation</h3>
                {c.situation.map((p) => (
                  <p class="type-body mt-md max-w-prose">{p}</p>
                ))}
              </div>

              <div>
                <h3 class="type-h3">What Rupert did</h3>
                <ol class="cs-steps">
                  {c.steps.map((s, i) => (
                    <li class="cs-step">
                      <span class="cs-step__num">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, "0")}</span>
                      <span>
                        <span class="cs-step__title">{s.title}</span>
                        <span class="cs-step__text">{s.body}</span>
                      </span>
                    </li>
                  ))}
                </ol>
              </div>
            </div>

            {c.quote && (
              <blockquote class="cs-quote">
                <p>“{c.quote}”</p>
                <footer>{c.quoteBy}</footer>
              </blockquote>
            )}
          </article>
        </section>
      ))
    }

    <section class="site-wrap pb-2xl">
      <p class="type-body-sm text-muted max-w-prose">
        Every raise is different. Results depend on the company, the round and the market. See
        <a href={sitePath("/how-it-works/")}>the process</a> for how an engagement runs.
      </p>
    </section>

    <CtaBanner />
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<script>
  // Progressive enhancement: without JS every case shows; with JS, one round at a time.
  const buttons = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>(".cs-round"));
  const sections = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>(".cs-section"));
  const show = (round: string) => {
    buttons.forEach((b) => b.setAttribute("aria-pressed", String(b.dataset.round === round)));
    sections.forEach((s) => (s.hidden = s.dataset.round !== round));
  };
  const fromHash = () => {
    const h = location.hash.slice(1);
    const hit = sections.find((s) => s.id === h || s.dataset.round === h);
    return hit?.dataset.round;
  };
  if (buttons.length) {
    show(fromHash() || buttons[0].dataset.round || "");
    buttons.forEach((b) =>
      b.addEventListener("click", () => {
        const r = b.dataset.round || "";
        show(r);
        history.replaceState(null, "", `#${r}`);
      }),
    );
  }
</script>

<style>
  .cs-rounds {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 8px;
  }
  .cs-round {
    min-height: 44px;
    padding: 10px 18px;
    border-radius: 8px;
    border: 1px solid #e4e2de;
    background: #ffffff;
    color: #1a1a2e;
    font: inherit;
    font-size: 15px;
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: border-color 200ms ease, background 200ms ease, color 200ms ease;
  }
  .cs-round:hover { border-color: #b5935a; }
  .cs-round[aria-pressed="true"] {
    background: #1a1a2e;
    border-color: #1a1a2e;
    color: #ffffff;
  }
  .cs-round:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid #b5935a; outline-offset: 2px; }
  .cs-section[hidden] { display: none; }
  .cs-eyebrow {
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #7a5c28;
  }
  .cs-case {
    background: #ffffff;
    border: 1px solid #e4e2de;
    border-radius: 16px;
    padding: 28px 20px;
    position: relative;
  }
  .cs-case::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    left: 28px;
    right: 28px;
    top: 0;
    height: 2px;
    background: #b5935a;
    opacity: 0.55;
    border-radius: 0 0 2px 2px;
  }
  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .cs-case { padding: 48px; }
  }
  .cs-facts {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 12px;
    margin: 32px 0 0;
  }
  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .cs-facts { grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
  }
  .cs-fact {
    background: linear-gradient(90deg, #eaf3ee 0%, #eef4f3 100%);
    border: 1px solid #a9d6c3;
    border-radius: 8px;
    box-shadow: 0 8px 24px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.05);
    padding: 16px;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .cs-fact dt {
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #12806a;
  }
  .cs-fact dd {
    margin: 6px 0 0;
    font-size: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
    font-weight: 400;
    color: #1a1a2e;
  }
  .cs-fact--result {
    grid-column: span 2;
    background: linear-gradient(90deg, #d9ede3 0%, #e2f0ec 100%);
    border-color: #8fcbb4;
  }
  .cs-fact--result dd { color: #12806a; }
  .cs-body {
    display: grid;
    gap: 40px;
    margin-top: 48px;
  }
  @media (min-width: 1024px) {
    .cs-body { grid-template-columns: 5fr 7fr; gap: 64px; }
  }
  .cs-steps {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 16px 0 0;
  }
  .cs-step {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 36px 1fr;
    gap: 12px;
    padding: 18px 0;
    border-top: 1px solid #e4e2de;
  }
  .cs-step:last-child { border-bottom: 1px solid #e4e2de; }
  .cs-step__num {
    font-family: "IBM Plex Mono", "Courier New", monospace;
    font-size: 12px;
    color: #7a5c28;
    padding-top: 4px;
  }
  .cs-step__title {
    display: block;
    font-size: 16px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: #1a1a2e;
  }
  .cs-step__text {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 4px;
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: #2d2d2d;
  }
  .cs-quote {
    margin: 48px 0 0;
    padding: 32px;
    background: linear-gradient(90deg, #eaf3ee 0%, #eef4f3 100%);
    border-left: 2px solid #12806a;
    border-radius: 4px;
  }
  .cs-quote p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 21px;
    line-height: 1.55;
    font-weight: 300;
    font-style: italic;
    color: #1a1a2e;
    max-width: 52ch;
  }
  .cs-quote footer {
    margin-top: 14px;
    font-size: 14px;
    color: #4a5568;
  }
</style>
